WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.958
In this simulation, a checkout release goes wrong.

00:00:04.138 --> 00:00:06.943
Follow the error rate as the team restores service.

00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:10.392
At ten o’clock, version 42 goes live.

00:00:10.572 --> 00:00:14.283
Before the release, two out of every
thousand requests failed.

00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:18.369
Three minutes later, eight out of every
hundred requests fail.

00:00:18.549 --> 00:00:20.841
The jump starts just after the deployment.

00:00:21.191 --> 00:00:22.955
The team pauses the rollout.

00:00:23.135 --> 00:00:27.428
They switch traffic back to version 41,
the last healthy release.

00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:31.987
After the rollback, the error rate
falls to 0.2 percent.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.176
It stays there for five minutes.

00:00:34.526 --> 00:00:37.424
That five-minute window now matches the baseline.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.225
Checkout is healthy again.
